---
// Marc's story, drafted from docs/ABOUT.md for him to change into his own words.
import { Picture } from "astro:assets";
import BaseLayout from "../layouts/BaseLayout.astro";
import NextSteps from "../components/NextSteps.astro";
import PageHeader from "../components/PageHeader.astro";
// The channel's banner: made by Marc in Canva, its two gamers drawn by Google's Gemini (CREDITS.md). Never served
// wider than 1280 pixels, so the whole banner stays inside Canva's 480,000-pixel limit for its Pro pictures.
import banner from "../assets/brand/charddie-games-banner.png";
import { links, pages } from "../lib/site";
---

<BaseLayout title="About" description="Why CF Gaming exists: a family's Windows games on their Macs, then the classic consoles.">
  <PageHeader title="About CF Gaming" lead="Why I made it, and what it's for." />

  <div class="wrap narrow stack story">
    <section class="glass panel" aria-labelledby="at-home">
      <h2 id="at-home">It began at home</h2>
      <p>
        My sons wanted to play their Windows games on their Macs, DirectX 12 ones included. Nothing we tried did all of it
        simply, so I built CF Gaming: its own Wine engine, made from CodeWeavers' open source, with Apple's D3DMetal for
        DirectX 12, and Steam in a case of its own, everything set up for them.
      </p>
    </section>

    <section class="glass panel" aria-labelledby="channel">
      <h2 id="channel">Charddie Games</h2>
      <Picture
        src={banner}
        alt="Charddie Games' banner: two cartoon gamers, one with a football and one with a toy blaster, beside the words Charddie Games and Let's Play."
        width={1280}
        widths={[640, 960, 1280]}
        sizes="(min-width: 48rem) 42rem, calc(100vw - 5rem)"
        formats={["avif", "webp"]}
        loading="lazy"
        decoding="async"
        class="banner"
      />
      <p>
        Follow my two sons' YouTube channel, if you'd like to: they like to play games and football, and other things
        occasionally.
      </p>
      <a class="button button-glass" href={links.charddieGames}>Charddie Games on YouTube</a>
    </section>

    <section class="glass panel" aria-labelledby="consoles">
      <h2 id="consoles">Then the consoles</h2>
      <p>
        Once the Windows games played, the old consoles followed: RetroArch and its cores, set up by CF Gaming, with each
        console's controller, memory cards, cheats, texture packs, and settings of its own for every game. Mac games and
        other emulators sit beside them.
      </p>
    </section>

    <section class="glass panel" aria-labelledby="one-place">
      <h2 id="one-place">One place, set up for a family</h2>
      <p>
        Every game on the Mac in one place, with nothing to configure by hand, calm words, and help built in. It's free,
        with no adverts, and it says plainly what it does and what it doesn't do yet.
      </p>
      <p class="signature">Marc</p>
    </section>
  </div>

  <NextSteps items={[pages.beforeYouStart, pages.install, pages.licences]} />
</BaseLayout>

<style>
  .story p {
    font-size: 1.12rem;
  }

  .story :global(.banner) {
    display: block;
    width: 100%;
    height: auto;
    margin-bottom: 1.25rem;
    border-radius: var(--radius-card);
  }

  .signature {
    margin-top: 1.5rem;
    font-weight: 700;
  }
</style>
